# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | In Progress          |

Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and does not invoke the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L10); [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` and emits a rejection log naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither output contains the offending property value ([validated by: logs the rejected field and expected type without logging its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L60); [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
- When an `enum` constraint rejects a property, the rejection names the property path and the `enum` constraint without exposing the rejected value ([validated by: names an enum constraint without exposing the rejected value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L35)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with an unknown property to the executor unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L97)).
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: compiles a static schema at registration and names the tool when the schema is invalid](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L120); [validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema`.
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: lets the model correct a schema-rejected tool call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L402); [validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
import {jest} from '@jest/globals';

import {setLogger} from '../../shared/logger.js';
import {ToolRegistry} from './registry.js';

describe('ToolRegistry', () => {
  afterEach(() => setLogger(undefined));

  // specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#1
  it('returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and does not invoke the executor', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'sunny');
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'get_weather',
        description: 'Get weather for a location',
        inputSchema: {
          type: 'object',
          properties: {location: {type: 'string'}},
          required: ['location'],
        },
      },
      executor
    );

    const response = await registry.execute('get_weather', {});

    expect({result: response.result, executorCalls: executor.mock.calls}).toEqual({
      result: expect.stringMatching(/location.*required|required.*location/i),
      executorCalls: [],
    });
  });

  // specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#3
  it('names an enum constraint without exposing the rejected value', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'unreachable');
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'get_weather',
        description: 'Get weather for a location',
        inputSchema: {
          type: 'object',
          properties: {units: {type: 'string', enum: ['metric', 'imperial']}},
        },
      },
      executor
    );

    const response = await registry.execute('get_weather', {units: 'private-units'});

    expect({
      mentionsConstraint: /units.*enum|enum.*units/i.test(response.result),
      leaksValue: response.result.includes('private-units'),
      executorCalls: executor.mock.calls,
    }).toEqual({mentionsConstraint: true, leaksValue: false, executorCalls: []});
  });

  // specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#2
  it('logs the rejected field and expected type without logging its value', async () => {
    const logInfo = jest.fn();
    setLogger({debug: jest.fn(), info: logInfo, warn: jest.fn(), error: jest.fn()});
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'unreachable');
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'lookup',
        description: 'Look up an identifier',
        inputSchema: {type: 'object', properties: {identifier: {type: 'string'}}},
      },
      executor
    );

    const response = await registry.execute('lookup', {identifier: 8675309});

    const logOutput = JSON.stringify(logInfo.mock.calls);
    expect({
      resultMentionsField: response.result.includes('identifier'),
      resultMentionsExpectedType: response.result.includes('string'),
      resultLeaksValue: response.result.includes('8675309'),
      logsMentionField: logOutput.includes('identifier'),
      logsMentionExpectedType: logOutput.includes('string'),
      logsLeakValue: logOutput.includes('8675309'),
      executorCalls: executor.mock.calls,
    }).toEqual({
      resultMentionsField: true,
      resultMentionsExpectedType: true,
      resultLeaksValue: false,
      logsMentionField: true,
      logsMentionExpectedType: true,
      logsLeakValue: false,
      executorCalls: [],
    });
  });

  // specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#4
  it('passes valid input with an unknown property to the executor unchanged exactly once', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'sunny');
    const input = {location: 'Berlin', requestId: 'weather-123'};
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'get_weather',
        description: 'Get weather for a location',
        inputSchema: {
          type: 'object',
          properties: {location: {type: 'string'}},
          required: ['location'],
        },
      },
      executor
    );

    await registry.execute('get_weather', input);

    expect(executor.mock.calls).toEqual([[input, undefined]]);
  });

  // specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#5
  it('compiles a static schema at registration and names the tool when the schema is invalid', () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const invalidDefinition = {
      name: 'broken_weather',
      description: 'Has an invalid JSON Schema type',
      inputSchema: {type: 'object', properties: {location: {type: 'not-a-json-schema-type'}}},
    };

    expect(() => registry.register(invalidDefinition, async () => 'unreachable')).toThrow(/broken_weather/);
  });
